 "note": "Loeffel et al. (2026, WCD 7, 895-913, Sect. 2) initialise every spin-off 'at the SSW onset or the day before', onset being the first day the daily-mean u(10 hPa, 60N) is negative. Six ensembles whose ensemble-mean wind is already negative at t = 0 therefore start on their onset day, and the registered rule (first negative ensemble-mean wind) anchors all 18 within 0-1.25 days: it is the primary estimate. A code review (2026-10-02) had read t = 0 as 'no onset in record' and kept only the 12 westerly-to-easterly crossings; that reading ignored the published design and was reverted the same day. The 12-event subset is kept as a sensitivity."
